& [SJS]
  + Situation: discovery and custody inspection validate separately but no single artifact proves the zero-knowledge staged entry path
  + Justification: a composed witness verifies roots and handles carry stable identity across tool stages while attention receives only compact metadata
  + Solution: generate bootstrap discovery pinned exact rediscovery and inspect as one digest-bound provider-free workflow

& [Delineation]
  + deterministic first-handle selection is fixture policy rather than semantic relevance
  + protocol composition is not live model tool choice or reflection quality
  + witness embeds requests and compact responses but no full checkpoint or transport bodies
  + all execution remains pure and provider-free

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + each stage uses the existing strict typed validator
  + root handle entry digest and inspection metadata equality close cross-stage identity
  + workflow digest commits the complete ordered witness excluding only itself

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty separates protocol composition from live inference and semantic relevance
  + Security binds every cross-stage root handle entry and response digest
  + Planner fixes bootstrap pin rediscover inspect order
  + Weaver demonstrates staged unfolding across two tools
  + Scribe preserves the complete compact public workflow
  + Refiner excludes full custody and transport bodies
  + Observer regenerates and mutates the whole witness

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated witness generator validator serializer artifact CLI and adversarial tests
  + keep live model reflection and semantic catalogue outside authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module artifact command exports and tests remove without changing predecessor behavior
